  '129': { name: 'Allura Red AC', cls: 'Colour — synthetic azo dye', verdict: 'bad', risk: 'high', organs: { brain: 3, gut: 2, immune: 2 }, harm: 'The most-used red azo dye. Linked to hyperactivity in children; 2022 research showed chronic exposure disrupts the gut barrier and promotes colitis-like inflammation in mice via serotonin signalling.', symptoms: 'Hyperactivity, hives, gut flare-ups in IBD-prone people', adi: '7 mg/kg bw/day', law: 'EU warning label mandatory; was banned in Denmark, Belgium, France and Switzerland pre-harmonisation.' },
